<title>GERMANY: Car rental group Sixt sales, earnings up. [Corrected 11:29 GMT]</title>
<headline>Car rental group Sixt sales, earnings up. [Corrected 11:29 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PULLACH, Germany 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German car rental group Sixt AG said on Monday that sales and earnings were up in the first five months of the year and predicted that car rental sales (corrects to read sales not income) would be at least 900 million marks ($518.5 million) in 1997.</p>
<p>That compares to car rental turnover (corrects from earnings) of 753 million marks in 1996, the company said, adding that it would add 90,000 cars to its fleet this year at a cost of 2.5 billion marks. ($ = 1.735 German Marks)</p>
</text>
